nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}}
What it does: {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Product: {{inputs.product}}
What they expect before opening: {{inputs.expectation}}
The detail worth noticing: {{inputs.detail}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast ONE person from the target audience and write a 3-beat unboxing they film themselves: beat 1 is the sealed parcel and the doubt, beat 2 is it open and the detail up close, beat 3 is the product in use and the CTA.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific room with named objects in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the opening frame: this person holding the unopened parcel, looking into the lens. Describe the person, the parcel, the room and the light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction on the master frame, not a new scene. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes, same room." then change only what their hands hold, their expression and the framing. Beat 2 comes in closer on the object; beat 3 pulls back and warms up.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 6 seconds AFTER that frame — the hands, the object and the delivery. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 14 words so it fits in 6 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: one caption per beat, at most 5 words each.
